('7cc10a8a-7991-5925-8913-f2716da522cc'::uuid,'est','"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In circle E below, ∠AEB ≅ ∠CED.\n[Figure: Circle with center E; A at top, D at bottom (AD a diameter-like vertical chord through E), B and C on the right side; radii EB and EC drawn.]\nBased on this information, which statement must be true?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"AB ≅ CD"},{"key":"G","text":"EB ⊥ EC"},{"key":"H","text":"m∠AED = 4(m∠DEC)"},{"key":"J","text":"m∠AEB + m∠DEC = m∠BEC"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh_geo.md","source_sha256":"fd550cf9acb0c34c08b3bebd88f0b67714179fd7b1d4644f694d4388df535983","source_question_id":"MG-24","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/MG-24.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for MG-24","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"F"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh_geo.md (MG-24)."'::jsonb),
